# Documentation sources of truth

Read `roadmap.md` before starting a feature, picking next work, or claiming
something is done. Follow `docs/principles.md` for how it should look and
behave.

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `roadmap.md` | Scheduled work (Now, phases, vis-*, leftovers, landed) |
| `issues.md` | Open bugs; include phase/action id when one exists |
| `backlog.md` | Unassigned ideas only — not the task list |
| `docs/coverage.md` | Casio feature coverage |
| `docs/visual-fidelity-inventory.md` | LCD element audit |
| `docs/prompts/tech-debt.md` | Now kickoff index (one slice per chat) |

- Update the matching `.md` file in the same change when you add, finish,
  defer, or close work.
- Canvases (`canvases/*.canvas.tsx`) are visual views. If they disagree with
  markdown, markdown wins — refresh the canvas when the story changed.
- Do not recreate a competing task list in chat, a canvas, or the README.
